# A 64-bit setp on %tid.x << 54, at least 2^63 from thread 512 on:
# ptxas skips the store on thread 0 alone. The comparison reads in
# i128, 18014398509481984 * %tid.x > 0, so of the CTA's 1024 threads
# the store runs on 1023 in 32 warps, not the 511 an i64 reading left
# positive, and the CTA stores 4092 B.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/setp_u64_wide.ptx | FileCheck --check-prefix=ANN "%s"
ANN: {{^}}.visible .entry micro_setp_u64_wide( // block 1024×1×1 | per CTA: global store 4,092 B; param load 8,192 B{{$}}
ANN: {{^}}	@%p1 st.global.u32 	[%rd5], %r1; // warp 0 × lane 1-31 ∪ warp 1-31 × lane * | exec 1,023/CTA | global store [4·%tid.x + param_0] sectors/req 4–5 (ideal 4){{$}}
